    },
    {
      "predicate": "iadas:authorConclusion",
      "object": "After controlling for age and the BMI, social physique anxiety was related to the EDI accounting for 4% to 13% of the variance in five of the eight subscales. There is a positive correlation between SPA and maturity fears, bulimia and two EDI social adjustement. There is negative correlations between the EDI subscales and physical self perceptions indicated that skaters less satisfied with their physical characteristics reported higher EDI scores. Physical self perception explained a significant portion of the variance in each EDI subscale after controlling for age and body size. Satisfaction with body fat predicted both drive for thinness and body dissatisfaction."
    },
    {
      "predicate": "iadas:perspectives",
      "object": "Future investigations should consider information on male partners and the potential mediating effects of SPA and self concept in the development of disordered eating. Maintaining or improving physical self perceptions may be an important foundation in the prevention of eating disorders, especially with skaters who skate with male partners."
    },
